   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The strong ending of the adjective",
     "texto": [
      "In the absence of an article, the adjective takes the same terminal endings that characterise the definite article **der/die/das** (with the only exception of the masculine and neuter genitive singular, which prefers **-en** because the noun carries the marker **-(e)s**): **frischer Kaffee** (der Kaffee), **kaltes Wasser** (das Wasser), **frische Milch** (die Milch), **warme Brötchen** (die Brötchen).",
      "In the oblique cases, the strong marker transfers entirely to the adjective: **mit frischem Kaffee** (masculine dative: -em like «dem»), **bei schlechtem Wetter** (neuter dative: -em), **nach harter Arbeit** (feminine dative: -er like «der»), **aus verlässlichen Quellen** (plural dative: -en)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
